# Python Automation System

## Overview

This is a Python-based automation framework that executes tasks dynamically from a JSON configuration file. It supports file creation, shell command execution, logging, and email automation with a scheduler system.

---

## Features

* JSON-based task configuration
* File creation automation
* Shell command execution
* Email automation (SMTP Gmail)
* Logging system
* Interval & timeout scheduler
* CLI-based control system

---

## Installation

### 1. Clone project

```
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/automation-system.git
```

### 2. Install dependencies

```
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

## Usage

Run the application:

```
python main.py
```

or

```
py -m configParser.config_parser
```

---

## Commands

| Command | Description             |
| ------- | ----------------------- |
| start   | Start automation system |
| stop    | Stop all running tasks  |
| restart | Restart system          |
| exit    | Exit application        |

---

## Configuration Example

```json
{
  "task_name": "example",
  "task_type": "shell",
  "schedule": {
    "type": "interval",
    "seconds": 5
  },
  "command": "echo Hello"
}
```

